  "final_message": "**Status:** Reproduced\n\n**Expected:** `<template #_slot2>` passed to `SubComponent` replaces that component's `<slot name=\"_slot2\">` fallback, as in v3.5.13.\n\n**Actual:** The fallback is rendered instead. The `#slot1` template, which has no underscore, still renders. Output at this revision:\n`<div><p>conditional</p><div style=\"color: green\">slot1 template works</div><div style=\"color: red\">default _slot2</div></div>`\n\n**Trigger:** A component with an underscore-named slot (`_slot2`) sits inside the default slot of a parent. That parent also receives a conditional `<template v-if=... #name>` slot, which makes its slots dynamic. Removing the `v-if`, or removing the wrapping `BaseLayout`, makes `_slot2` render correctly. Slot names are `slot1` and `_slot2` in the 3.5.13 link, and `title` and `_duration` in the 3.5.14 link. I used `_slot2`.\n\n**Run:** `npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts` from the repo root. It exits 1 now and asserts only that the `_slot2` template content is rendered and the fallback is not.\n\n**Passes when:**\n- A throwaway edit to `assignSlots` in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts` makes the test pass (exit 0). I changed `!isInternalKey(key)` back to `key !== '_'` and then reverted it. `git status` shows only the new test file.\n- Published `vue@3.5.13` renders `_slot2 template works`, using the same components and scenario in a standalone jsdom script. `vue@3.5.14` and `vue@3.5.17` render the fallback.\n\n**Likely cause:** `assignSlots` in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts` skips every key starting with `_` when `optimized` is false. The parent's dynamic slots make the Fragment from `renderSlot` use the BAIL patch flag, so the child mounts with `optimized=false` and `_slot2` is never copied. Before 5d166f3 the check was `key !== '_'`.\n\n**Artifacts:**\n- The test is `/work/runs/f2c75c31a1/repo/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts`. Its components are compiled at runtime from the report's template source. I compiled the report's real `App.vue` with `compiler-sfc` and its slot structure matches (`_duration` slot, `_: 1` STABLE, outer `_createSlots`).\n- Scratch files are in `/tmp/f2c75c31a1/pub`.\n\nNo production code was changed. Separately, `/tmp/rc/pub/scenario.cjs` was already on disk from some other run. I read it in passing, did not use it, and did not touch the path it points to.\n",
  "run_command": "npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..ed5853d\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@\n+import { createApp } from '../src'\n+\n+// Reproduction of: \"Slot <template> not working when its name starts with an\n+// underscore (_) since v3.5.14\".\n+//\n+// Components mirror the report (BaseLayout.vue, SubComponent.vue, App.vue),\n+// compiled at runtime from the same template source.\n+describe('slot names starting with an underscore', () => {\n+  it('renders `#_slot2` content instead of the slot fallback when SubComponent is a sibling of a conditional slot template of BaseLayout', () => {\n+    const BaseLayout = {\n+      template: `\n+        <div>\n+          <slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot>\n+          <slot></slot>\n+        </div>\n+      `,\n+    }\n+\n+    const SubComponent = {\n+      template: `\n+        <slot name=\"slot1\">\n+          <div style=\"color: red\">default slot content for slot1</div>\n+        </slot>\n+        <slot name=\"_slot2\">\n+          <div style=\"color: red\">default slot content for _slot2</div>\n+        </slot>\n+      `,\n+    }\n+\n+    const App = {\n+      components: { BaseLayout, SubComponent },\n+      data() {\n+        return { anyConditionCheckHereWillDo: true }\n+      },\n+      template: `\n+        <BaseLayout>\n+          <template v-if=\"anyConditionCheckHereWillDo\" #randomslotname>\n+            <p>conditionally rendered slot</p>\n+          </template>\n+\n+          <SubComponent>\n+            <template #slot1>\n+              <div style=\"color: green\">slot1 template works</div>\n+            </template>\n+\n+            <template #_slot2>\n+              <div style=\"color: green\">_slot2 template works</div>\n+            </template>\n+          </SubComponent>\n+        </BaseLayout>\n+      `,\n+    }\n+\n+    const container = document.createElement('div')\n+    createApp(App).mount(container)\n+    const html = container.innerHTML\n+\n+    // sanity: the slot without the underscore prefix is rendered fine\n+    expect(html).toContain('slot1 template works')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('default slot content for slot1')\n+\n+    // expected (as in v3.5.13): the `_slot2` template replaces the fallback\n+    expect(html).toContain('_slot2 template works')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('default slot content for _slot2')\n+  })\n+})\n"
}
